\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% TRANSFORMATION TNoControl
< m1: CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ I1:mu1,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu2],
             mu3
           ]
>

< m : CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ I1:mu1,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu2],
             mu3
           ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: NOT EXIST (mu1, [ I11:rel1/SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu1, [ I12:rel1/NP{NPrec1}[mu4]])
         I11: rel1 IN [leftdislocrel, subjrel] AND
              SENTENCErec1.PROsubject = true AND
              SENTENCErec1.adverbial = false
         I12: rel1 IN [leftdislocrel, subjrel] AND
              NPrec1.NPhead = openIngNP
       m1: EXIST (mu1, [auxrel/I25::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu6]]) 
           OR 
           (
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [ I21:rel2/T1]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [prepobjrel/PREPP{PREPPrec1}
                                      [ head/PREP{},
                                        I21:objrel/T1]]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [prepobjrel/PREPP{PREPPrec1}
                                      [ head/PREP{},
                                        objrel/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]
                                      ] ]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [predrel/I23::N1
                                   [ mu5,
                                     I24:rel2/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4],
                                     mu6
                                   ] ]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [complrel/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu3, [extraposrel/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]])
           )
       m : EXIST (mu1, [auxrel/I25::VERB{VERBrec1}[mu6]]) 
           OR 
           (
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [ I21:rel2/T1]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [prepobjrel/PREPP{PREPPrec1}
                                      [ head/PREP{},
                                        I21:objrel/T1]]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [prepobjrel/PREPP{PREPPrec1}
                                      [ head/PREP{},
                                        objrel/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]
                                      ] ]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [predrel/I23::N1
                                   [ mu5,
                                     I24:rel2/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4],
                                     mu6
                                   ] ]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu2, [complrel/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu3, [extraposrel/I22::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}[mu4]])
           )
         I21: T1.CAT IN AUX_xppropcatset OR
              ( T1.CAT IN [NP] WITH T1.REC.NPhead = OpenIngNP )
         I22: SENTENCErec1.PROsubject = true AND
              SENTENCErec1.adverbial = false
         I23: N1.CAT IN [ADJP, NP, PREPP, ADVP]
         I24: rel2 IN [toinfmodrel, complrel, postadjrel,
                       causadvrel, toinfcomplrel, resultrel]
         I25: VERBrec1.subc = modalverb
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
&
\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TNoControl
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
\begin{enumerate}
\item No embedded sentence:\\
He did [leave], he did [go to the movies]
\item Closed subjrel/SENTENCE or leftdislocrel/SENTENCE:\\
That he went away so early do [surprise me]\\
How the book will sell do [depend on its author]\\
?Eating people is not [good for your appetite]
\item Closed SENTENCE in the VERBP (both finite and infinite):\\
a. (prep)CLOSEDGERUND: x1 do [watch [the moon rising over the mountains 
yesterday]]; x1 do [count on [the weather being fine]]\\
b. (prep)CLOSEDTOSENT: x1 do [expect [he to go]]; x1 do [count on [you to
help]]\\
c. CLOSEDINFSENT: x1 do [see [he leave]]\\
d. FORTOSENT: x1 do [prefer [for John to go]]\\
e. 0-THATSENT: x1 do [discover [his colleages lied to him] yesterday]
\item Closed extraposed SENTENCE (always finite)\\
a. ASIFSENT: -- do [appear] yesterday [as if she'd win]; x1 do [act] yesterday
[as if he had gone mad]\\
b. QSENT: x1 do [hesitate] yesterday [what she would do now]\\
c. THATSENT: x1 do [know] [that he'll come]
\end{enumerate}
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_Controlrules
\item[* date of creation:] 23-FEB-1988
\item[* author:] Margreet Sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch TControl0
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 10/04/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted rule to stop SENTENCEs under predrel/XP in the VERBP too.
\item date: 25/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted rule to allow complrel/SENTENCE to pass if the subjVAR has already been 
deleted in a previous cycle (i.e. when the aux now is a modalverb)
\item date: 2/11/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Adapted rule to allow {\em anything } to pass if there is a modal. Also adapted 
all other control rules to stop modals there (only needed to speed up analysis,
not crucial).
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To let clauses not containing XPPROPs or certain embedded 
sentences pass the control rules. 
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
It is assumed that \\
1. open sentences in subject position (leftdislocrel, or perhaps subjrel -- 
for open gerunds: Eating people is wrong -- ) 
need control; howvever, the relevant rules (always NOC) have not been written 
yet, so that these sentences will not pass this TC yet (To kill someone is a 
crime; How to behave should be learned at home)\\
2. sentences that occur as the obj of a byobjrel/PREPP will always be finite, 
and will never need control (I was amazed by what they wanted of me)\\
3. closed SENTENCEs in the VERBP (either within a PREPP or not) do not need 
any structural change; this means that objective case must also be assigned to 
what still is the subject of an embedded clause.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] none
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
The verb `regard as' is now also covered by the NoControl rules (TNoControl for 
sentence complements, TNoControlPrepXP for proposition complements), since 
the verb is considered two-place, thus taking closed complements. This means 
that the incorrect constituent order {\em regard as him being without 
principles\/} is still allowed. A solution would be to accpet `regard as' as a 
three place verb with object control. This seems to cause translation problems, 
however. The alternative is to add an English rule which applies only to `as', 
and moves its embedded subject out of the prepp. Note that TNoControlPrepPREPP 
is written solely for cases with `as', and should be changed if a three place 
verb `regard as' is recognised.
\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}

\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TOblObjControlADJP   (* openadjpprop, obj control *)
< m1: CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
            [ I1:mu1,
              predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                    [ mu2,
                      objrel/T1,
                      mu3,
                      complrel/OPENADJPPROP{OPENADJPPROPrec1}
                              [ subjrel/T2,
                                predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}[mu4] 
                              ],
                      mu5 
                    ],
               mu6
            ]
>

< m : CLAUSE{CLAUSErec2}
            [ I1:mu1,
              predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                    [ mu2,
                      objrel/T1,
                      mu3,
                      predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}[mu4], 
                      mu5 
                    ],
              mu6
            ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: NOT EXIST (mu1, [I11:auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu11]])
         I11: VERBrec1.subc = modalverb
      >

<
   SUBRULE (* 1. NPVAR *)
      < T1: NPVAR{NPVARrec1} 
        T2: NPVAR{NPVARrec2} >
      < T1: NPVAR{NPVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: NPVARrec1 = NPVARrec2 AND 
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 = COPYT_adjpTOadjpprop(ADJPrec1) 
                EXCEPT FOR [aktionsarts, superdeixis, PROsubject]
              AND
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 = { aktionsarts   : [stative] 
                                   superdeixis   : omegadeixis
                                   PROsubject    : true } 
              C11: CLAUSErec1.synvpefs * AUX_openxppvps <> [] 
              A11: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
              C12: CLAUSErec1.adjuncts * [resAP] <> []
              A12: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
              C11:CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_openxppvps <> [] 
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.synvpefs := 
                       CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_openxppvps;
              C12: CLAUSErec2.adjuncts * [resAP] <> []
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
          A1: NPVARrec2 := NPVARrec1;
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 := COPYT_adjpTOadjpprop(ADJPrec1); 
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 := { aktionsarts   : [stative ]
                                    superdeixis   : omegadeixis
                                    PROsubject    : true }

         >

   SUBRULE (* 2. CNVAR *)
      < T1: CNVAR{CNVARrec1} 
        T2: CNVAR{CNVARrec2} >
      < T1: CNVAR{CNVARrec1} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: CNVARrec1 = CNVARrec2 AND 
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 = COPYT_adjpTOadjpprop(ADJPrec1) 
                EXCEPT FOR [aktionsarts, superdeixis, PROsubject]
              AND
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 = { aktionsarts   : [stative] 
                                   superdeixis   : omegadeixis
                                   PROsubject    : true }
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
              C11:CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_openxppvps <> [] 
              A11: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
                   CLAUSErec1.synvpefs := 
                       CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_openxppvps;
              C12: CLAUSErec2.adjuncts * [resAP] <> []
              A12: CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
          A1: CNVARrec2 := CNVARrec1;
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 := COPYT_adjpTOadjpprop(ADJPrec1); 
              OPENADJPPROPrec1 := { aktionsarts   : [stative ]
                                    superdeixis   : omegadeixis
                                    PROsubject    : true }
         >
>
&

\end{verbatim}
