\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TNoControlPrepADJP  (* prepobjrel/CLOSEDADJPPROP *)
< m1: CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
            [ I3:mu1,
              predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                     [ I1:mu2,
                       prepobjrel/PREPP{PREPPrec1}
                                 [ head/PREP{PREPrec1},
                                   objrel/CLOSEDADJPPROP{CLOSEDADJPPROPrec1}
                                         [ I2:subjrel/T1,
                                           predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}[mu4]
                                         ]
                                 ],
                       mu5
                     ],
              mu6
            ]
>

< m : CLAUSE{CLAUSErec2}
            [ I3:mu1,
              predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                     [ I1:mu2,
                       I2:objrel/T1,
                       prepobjrel/PREPP{PREPPrec2}
                                 [ head/PREP{PREPrec1},
                                   predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}[mu4]
                                 ],
                       mu5
                     ],
              mu6
            ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: NOT EXIST (mu2, [objrel/..])
       I2: T1.CAT IN [NP, NPVAR, CNVAR]
       I3: NOT EXIST (mu1, [I31:auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu11]])
         I31: VERBrec1.subc = modalverb
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: CLOSEDADJPPROPrec1 = COPYT_adjpTOadjpprop(ADJPrec1) 
                   EXCEPT FOR [aktionsarts, superdeixis, PROsubject] 
              (* req and env are assumed the same as in ADJP *)
              AND
              CLOSEDADJPPROPrec1 = { aktionsarts   : [stative]
                                     superdeixis   : omegadeixis
                                     PROsubject    : false } AND
              CLAUSErec1.synvpefs * AUX_closedxppvps <> [] 
              (* no example of EMPTY_PREPCLOSEDADJPPROP known *)
          A1: PREPPrec2 := PREPPrec1
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_closedxppvps <> []
          A1: CLOSEDADJPPROPrec1 := COPYT_adjpTOadjpprop(ADJPrec1);
              CLOSEDADJPPROPrec1 := { aktionsarts   : [stative]
                                      superdeixis   : omegadeixis
                                      PROsubject    : false } ;
              CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
              CLAUSErec1.synvpefs := 
                  CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_closedxppvps;
              PREPPrec1 := PREPPrec2
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TNoControlPrepADJP
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
(vp012): ?strike x3 as [he pompous] $\rightarrow$ strike x3 he as pompous
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_Controlrules
\item[* date of creation:]   01-MAR-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch TNoControl2
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 01/06/90\ \ \ \ \ author:Petra de Wit
replaced specific pattern(s) by set of CLOSED verbpatterns
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To remove the CLOSEDADJPPROP node that is in a prepobjrel, 
and to turn its subject into an objrel/.. of the higher clause
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:] 
The subdivision into subrules has been removed. It was argumented as follows:\\
There is a subrule for the case that T1 is an NP, and one for where this is not
the case.
If T1 is an NP, then the req of ADJPPROP equals the most 'dominant' one of
NPrec1.req and ADJPrec1.req (where pospol,negpol 'more dominant' than 
[pospol, negpol, Omegapol]).
If no distinction in dominancy can be made, the two relevant values must be 
the same.\\
If T1 is an NPVAR or a CNVAR, the req-values of these constituents do not 
codetermine the value of the req attribute of the CLOSEDADJPPROP. 
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] none
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\
\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}

