\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TNoControlNP       (* closed NPPROP *)
< m1:CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ I3:mu1,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                    [ I1:mu2,
                      complrel/CLOSEDNPPROP{CLOSEDNPPROPrec1}
                              [ I2:subjrel/T1,
                                predrel/NP{NPrec1}[mu3] 
                              ],
                      mu4
                    ],
             mu5
           ]
>

< m :CLAUSE{CLAUSErec2}
           [ I3:mu1,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                    [ I1:mu2,
                      I2:objrel/T1,
                      predrel/NP{NPrec1}[mu3],
                      mu4
                    ],
             mu5
           ]
>
   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: NOT EXIST (mu2, [objrel/..])
       I2: T1.CAT IN [NP, NPVAR, CNVAR]
       I3: NOT EXIST (mu1, [I31:auxrel/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu11]])
         I31: VERBrec1.subc = modalverb
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: CLOSEDNPPROPrec1 = { superdeixis    : omegadeixis
                                   aktionsarts    : [stative]
                                   thetanp        : NPrec1.thetanp
                                   nounpatternefs : NPrec1.nounpatternefs
                                   PROsubject     : false } AND
              (* no test on req and env *)
              CLAUSErec1.synvpefs * AUX_closedxppvps <> [] 
          A1: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_closedxppvps <> []
          A1: CLOSEDNPPROPrec1 := { thetanp        : NPrec1.thetanp
                                    nounpatternefs : NPrec1.nounpatternefs
                                    PROsubject     : false 
                                    aktionsarts    : [stative] }
              (* superdeixis retains default value *);
              CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
              CLAUSErec1.synvpefs :=
                CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * AUX_closedxppvps
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TNoControlNP
\item[* relevant examples:]\mbox{}\\
(vp010): become [she President] $\rightarrow$ become she President\\
(vp120): x1 consider [he a fool] $\rightarrow$ x1 consider he a fool\\
(vp012): seem [he a fool] x2 $\rightarrow$ seem he a fool x2
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_Controlrules
\item[* date of creation:] 01-MRT-1988
\item[* author:] Margreet Sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch TNoControl3
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 01/06/90\ \ \ \ \ author:Petra de Wit
replaced specific pattern(s) by set of CLOSED verbpatterns
\item date: 06/09/90\ \ \ \ \ author:Petra de Wit
analysis: changed value of PROsubject to FALSE in DECOMP
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To delete CLOSEDNPPROP, and to turn its subject into an object
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
The conditions on req and env have been removed. They were:\\
There is a subrule for the case that T1 is an NP, and one for where this is not
the case.
If T1 is an NP, then the req of CLOSEDNPPROP equals the most 'dominant' one of
NPrec2.req and NPrec1.req (where pospol,negpol 'more dominant' than 
[pospol, negpol, Omegapol]).
If no distinction in dominancy can be made, the two relevant values must be 
the same.\\
If T1 is an NPVAR or a CNVAR, the req of these constituents does not 
codetermine the value of the req attribute of the CLOSEDNPPROP. 
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\
It is assumed that extraposition inside the NPPROP has applied already, if 
necessary (so that no SENTENCE can be the subjrel/ of CLOSEDNPPROP), and that a 
dummy subject `it' has been inserted. No allowances have been made for NPPROPs 
which do not have a subject, or some other subject than an NP/CN(VAR)
\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
\item[\ \ remarks:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item problems:\\

\item modifications:\\

\end{enumerate}
\end{description}


